  "text": "**Cache Implementation - Review and Fixes:**\n\n**Original Implementation Issues:**\n1. Cache key included headers → would fragment cache massively\n2. Duplicate duration checks in HLS + PlaybackResolver\n3. R2 caching in legacy handler instead of edge cache\n4. OPTIONS responses not cached (unnecessary CORS preflight latency)\n\n**Fixes Applied:**\n- Cache key now URL-only (prevents fragmentation)\n- Removed HLS endpoint duration check (trust PlaybackResolver)\n- Simplified legacy UID handler (removed R2 caching)\n- Added OPTIONS caching (CORS preflight now 1-5ms instead of 50-200ms)\n- Improved logging (full pathnames instead of truncated)\n\n**Expected Performance After Fixes:**\n- Cache hit rate: >90% (was going to be ~30%)\n- Cache hits: 1-5ms (no Worker execution)\n- Cache misses: 50-200ms (full KV + R2)\n- OPTIONS preflight: 1-5ms cached (was 50-200ms every time)\n\n**Testing Checklist:**\n```bash\n# Verify cache hit rate\ncurl -I https://cdn.divine.video/{sha256}  # MISS\ncurl -I https://cdn.divine.video/{sha256}  # HIT\n\n# Verify no header fragmentation\ncurl -H \"User-Agent: A\" https://cdn.divine.video/{sha256}  # MISS\ncurl -H \"User-Agent: B\" https://cdn.divine.video/{sha256}  # HIT (same cache!)\n\n# Verify OPTIONS caching\ncurl -X OPTIONS https://cdn.divine.video/{sha256}  # MISS\ncurl -X OPTIONS https://cdn.divine.video/{sha256}  # HIT\n```\n\n**Monitoring After Deploy:**\n- Watch Cloudflare Analytics: subrequest count should drop 90-95%\n- Check logs for `[Cache HIT]` vs `[Cache MISS]` ratio\n- Verify cf-cache-status: HIT in response headers",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes"
  ],
